    and service roads are deliberately not in this graph, so a click in a
    city centre is often more than 45 m from the nearest rideable road.
    A map click should land on the nearest road there is, not fail.

    Answers through the bucket grid, expanding a ring at a time. Once a
    candidate is found it keeps going for as many more rings as could still
    hold something closer, so the result is EXACTLY the node the old full
    sweep returned, not merely a near one.
    """
    k = math.cos(math.radians(lat))
    gy, gx = int(lat / NODE_CELL_DEG), int(lon / NODE_CELL_DEG)
    best, best_d = None, float("inf")
